{
  "title": "26: al-Shoa'raa الشعراء",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nطٰسٓمّٓ‏(1)\nTaa Sim Meem.\nTa Seen Meem (T. S. M.)\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْنِ‏(2)\nTILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE MOBEEN.\nThese are the verses of the Book Manifest\nلَعَلَّكَ بَاخِعٌ نَّفْسَكَ اَلَّا يَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(3)\nLAA’ALLAKA BAAKHEA’UN NNAFSAKA ALLAA YAKOONOOA MUMENEENA.\nHapply thou wilt kill thyself with grief that they become not believers\nاِنْ نَّشَاْ نُنَزِّلْ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ اٰيَةً فَظَلَّتْ اَعْنَاقُهُمْ لَهَا خٰضِعِيْنَ‏(4)\nIN NASHAA NUNAZZEL A’LAYHIM MENAL SAMAAA-E AAYATAL FAZALLAT AAA’NAAQUHUM LAHAA KHAAZEE’EENA.\nIf We will, We can send down upon them from the heaven a sign that their necks get bent unto it.\nوَمَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ ذِكْرٍ مِّنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ مُحْدَثٍ اِلَّا كَانُوْا عَنْهُ مُعْرِضِيْنَ‏(5)\nWA MAA YAATEEHIM MIN ZEKRIN MENAL RAHMAANIR MUHDASIN ILLAA KAANOO A’NHO MOA’REZEEN.\nAnd there cometh not unto them of a reminder from the Beneficent (God) afresh, save they, from it, turn aside.\nفَقَدْ كَذَّبُوْا فَسَيَاْتِيْهِمْ اَنْۢبٰٓؤُا مَا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(6)\nFAQAD KAZZABOO FASAYAATEEHEM AANBAAAUA MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd indeed they belied it: but soon shall come unto them the tidings of what they mock (at).\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلَى الْاَرْضِ كَمْ اَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍ كَرِيْمٍ‏(7)\nAWALAM YARAW ELAL ARZE KAM AANBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE ZAWJIN KAREEM.\nWhat! See they not unto the earth, how many of every noble kind We have caused to grow in it?\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(8)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nVerily in that there is a sign; but most of them believe not.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(9)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nVerily thy Lord, certainly is He the Al-Mighty, the All- Merciful.\nوَاِذْ نَادٰى رَبُّكَ مُوْسٰۤى اَنِ ائْتِ الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(10)\nWA IZ NAADAA RABBOKA MOOSAA SAALEHAN ATE QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd when called out thy Lord unto Moses saying: “Go thou unto the unjust people (to guide them)?\nقَوْمَ فِرْعَوْنَ‌ؕ اَلَا يَتَّقُوْنَ‌‏(11)\nQAWMA FIR-A’WN ALAA YATTAQOON.\nThe people of Pharaoh; Will they not ward off evil?\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْنِؕ‏(12)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE AKHAAFO AN YYUKAZZEBOONE.\nSaid (Moses): “O’ my Lord! Verily fear I that they will belie me!\nوَيَضِيْقُ صَدْرِىْ وَلَا يَنْطَلِقُ لِسَانِىْ فَاَرْسِلْ اِلٰى هٰرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWAYAZEEQU SADREAA WA LAA YANTALEQU LESAANEAA FAARSEL ELAA AALO.\nAnd straitened is my breast, and eloquent is not my tongue, so send Thou unto Aaron (to my aid)\nوَلَهُمْ عَلَىَّ ذَنْۢبٌ فَاَخَافُ اَنْ يَّقْتُلُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(14)\nWA LAHUM A’LAYYA ZANBUN FA AKHAAFO AN YAQTOLOON.\nAnd they have (a charge) against me (of) a crime, and fear I that they may slay me.\nقَالَ كَلَّا‌ ۚ فَاذْهَبَا بِاٰيٰتِنَآ‌ اِنَّا مَعَكُمْ مُّسْتَمِعُوْنَ‏(15)\nQAALA KALLAA FAAZHABAA BE-AAYAATENAA INNAA MA-A’KUM MMUSTAMEU’OONA.\nSaid (God): “By no means! so go ye both with Our signs, Verily, with you are We, (and will be) hearing!\nفَاْتِيَا فِرْعَوْنَ فَقُوْلَاۤ اِنَّا رَسُوْلُ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(16)\nFAATEEA FIR-A’WNA FAQOOLAA INNAA RASOOLAL RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nSo go unto Pharaoh and say ye both (unto him): “Verily we two are the apostles of the Lord of the worlds!\nاَنْ اَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ؕ‏(17)\nAN AARSEL MAA’ANAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ.\nSend thou with us the children of Israel!\nقَالَ اَلَمْ نُرَبِّكَ فِيْنَا وَلِيْدًا وَّلَبِثْتَ فِيْنَا مِنْ عُمُرِكَ سِنِيْنَۙ‏(18)\nQAALA ALAM NURABBEKA FEENAA WALEEDAN WWALABESTA FEENAA MIN U’UMUREKA SENEEN.\nSaid (Pharaoh): “Did we not cherish thee amidst us as a child? And thou didst dwell amidst us for (many) years of thy life,\nوَفَعَلْتَ فَعْلَتَكَ الَّتِىْ فَعَلْتَ وَاَنْتَ مِنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(19)\nWAFAA’ALTA FAA’LATAKA LATEE FAA’ALTA WA ANTA MENAL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd thou (O’ Moses!) didst a deed which thou didst and thou art one of the ungrateful (ones).\nقَالَ فَعَلْتُهَاۤ اِذًا وَّاَنَا مِنَ الضَّآلِّيْنَؕ‏(20)\nQAALA FAA’ALTUHAA EZAL WWAANAA MENAL AZ-ZAALLEENA.\nSaid (Moses): “I did it while I was one not yet directed” (as what to do)\nفَفَرَرْتُ مِنْكُمْ لَمَّا خِفْتُكُمْ فَوَهَبَ لِىْ رَبِّىْ حُكْمًا وَّجَعَلَنِىْ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(21)\nFAFARARTU MINKUM LAMMAA KHEFTUKUM FAWAHABA LEE RABBEE HUKMAWN WWAJAA’ALANEAA MENAL MURSALEEN.\nSo I fled from you when I feared you, then granted unto me my Lord, command, and made me (one) of (His) apostles.\nوَتِلْكَ نِعْمَةٌ تَمُنُّهَا عَلَىَّ اَنْ عَبَّدْتَّ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ؕ‏(22)\nWA TILKAL NEA’MATUN TAMUNNUHAA A’LAYYA AN A’ABBADTTA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ.\nAnd is it a favour wherewith thou reproachest me: that thou hast enslaved the children of Israel?\nقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَا رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(23)\nQAALA FIRA’WNO WA MAA RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nSaid Pharaoh: “What is the Lord of the worlds?\nقَالَ رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَاؕ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّوْقِنِيْنَ‏(24)\nQAALA RABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHUMAA IN KUNTUM MOOQENEEN.\nSaid (Moses): “(He is) The Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is between the two, if only ye be sure.\nقَالَ لِمَنْ حَوْلَهٗۤ اَلَا تَسْتَمِعُوْنَ‏(25)\nQAALA LEMAN-Y HAWLAHU ALAA TASTAMEU’OONA.\nSaid (Pharaoh) unto those around him: “Do ye hear not?\nقَالَ رَبُّكُمْ وَرَبُّ اٰبَآئِكُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALA RABBOKUM WA RABBO AABAAA-EKOMUL AWWALEEN.\nSaid (Moses): “(God is) your Lord and the Lord of our fathers of old!\nقَالَ اِنَّ رَسُوْلَكُمُ الَّذِىْۤ اُرْسِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ لَمَجْنُوْنٌ‏(27)\nQAALA INNAL RASOOLAKUMU LAZEE AURSELA ELAYKUM LAMAJNOONUN.\nSaid (he): “Verily your apostle who is sent unto you is certainly mad.\nقَالَ رَبُّ الْمَشْرِقِ وَالْمَغْرِبِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا ؕ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(28)\nQAALA RABBUL MASHREQE WAL MAGHREBE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA IN KUNTUM TA’QELOON.\nSaid (Moses): “(God is) the Lord of the east and the west and what is between the two, if ye (only) understand\nقَالَ لَئِنِ اتَّخَذْتَ اِلٰهًا غَيْرِىْ لَاَجْعَلَنَّكَ مِنَ الْمَسْجُوْنِيْنَ‏(29)\nQAALA LAENE ATTAKHAZTA ELAAHANW GHAYREE LAAJA’ALANNAKA MENAL AL-MASJOONEENA.\nSaid (Pharaoh): “Should thou take a god other than me, I will certainly make thee one of the imprisoned ones.\nقَالَ اَوَلَوْ جِئْتُكَ بِشَىْءٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(30)\nQAALA LAW JE’TOKA BE-SHAY-IM MOBEEN.\nSaid (Moses): “What! even if I bring unto thee something manifest?\nقَالَ فَاْتِ بِهٖۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(31)\nQAALA FAATE BEHI IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nSaid (Pharaoh): “Bring it then, if thou be of the truthful ones.\n‌فَاَ لْقٰى عَصَاهُ فَاِذَا هِىَ ثُعْبَانٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ ۖ ‌‌ۚ‏(32)\nFA-ALQEEHE LQAA A’ASAAHU FA-EZAA HEYA SUA’BAANUN MOBEEN.\nSo he (Moses) threw down his staff, and lo! and it was a manifest serpent,\nوَّنَزَعَ يَدَهٗ فَاِذَا هِىَ بَيْضَآءُ لِلنّٰظِرِيْنَ‏(33)\nWWANAZAA’A YADAH FA-EZAA HEYA BAYZAAU LELNNAAZEREENA.\nAnd he drew out his hand, and lo! it was radiant white unto the beholders.\nقَالَ لِلْمَلَاِ حَوْلَهٗۤ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسٰحِرٌ عَلِيْمٌۙ‏(34)\nQAALA LIL-MALAA HAWLAHU INNAL HAAZAA LASAAHERUN A’LEEM.\nSaid (Pharaoh) unto the chiefs around him: “Verily this is a skilled sorcerer”,\nيُّرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّخْرِجَكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِكُمْ بِسِحْرِهٖ ‌ۖ  فَمَاذَا تَاْمُرُوْنَ‌‏(35)\nYYUREEDU AN YYUKHREJAKUM MIN AARZEKUM BESEHREH FA MAA TAAMUROONA.\nIntendeth he to drive you out of your land with his sorcery, what then is it ye counsel?\nقَالُوْۤا اَرْجِهْ وَاَخَاهُ وَابْعَثْ فِى الْمَدَآئِنِ حٰشِرِيْنَۙ‏(36)\nQAALOO AARJEH WAAKHAAHU WAB A’S FIL AL-MADAAENE HAASHEREENA.\nSaid they: “Give him respite and to his Brother (Aaron), and send heralds into the cities,\nيَاْتُوْكَ بِكُلِّ سَحَّارٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(37)\nYAATOOKA BEKULLE SAHHAARIN A’LEEM.\n(That) they bring unto thee all the sorcerers well-versed\nفَجُمِعَ السَّحَرَةُ لِمِيْقَاتِ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍۙ‏(38)\nFAJUMEA’A AS-SAHARATU LE-MEEQAATE YAWMIN MA’LOOM.\nSo were gathered together the sorcerers at the appointed time on a day (which was) announced,\nوَّقِيْلَ لِلنَّاسِ هَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّجْتَمِعُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nWWAQEELA LIN-NAASE HAL ANTUM MMUJTAMEU’OONA.\nAnd it was said unto the people: “Will ye all assemble?\nلَعَلَّنَا نَتَّبِعُ السَّحَرَةَ اِنْ كَانُوْا هُمُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَ‏(40)\nLAA’ALLANAA NATTA-BE-O’ AS-SAHARATA IN KAANOO HOMUL AL-GHAALEBEENA.\nHapply we may follow the sorcerers, if they be triumphant\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ السَّحَرَةُ قَالُوْا لِفِرْعَوْنَ اَئِنَّ لَنَا لَاَجْرًا اِنْ كُنَّا نَحْنُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَ‏(41)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AS-SAHARATU QAALOO LE-FIR-A’WNA AAENNA LANAA LAAJRAN IN KUNNAA NAHNO AL-GHAALEBEENA.\nWhen came the sorcerers, said they unto Pharaoh: “Is there for us a reward if we be triumphant?\nقَالَ نَعَمْ وَاِنَّكُمْ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ‏(42)\nQAALA NAA’AM WA INNAKUM EZAL LAMENAZ MOQARRABEEN.\nSaid (Pharaoh): “Yea! verily ye in that case be of those (exalted to be) nearest (to me)\nقَالَ لَهُمْ مُّوْسٰۤى اَلْقُوْا مَاۤ اَنْتُمْ مُّلْقُوْنَ‏(43)\nQAALA LAHUM MOOSAA AALQOOA MAA ANTUM MMULQOONA.\nSaid unto them Moses: “Cast ye what ye have to cast!\nفَاَلْقَوْا حِبَالَهُمْ وَعِصِيَّهُمْ وَقَالُوْا بِعِزَّةِ فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(44)\nFAALQAWA HEBAALAHUM WAE’ESEEHUM WA QAALOO BEE’EZZATE FIR-A’WNA INNAA LANAHNU GHAALEBOON.\nThen they cast down their cords and their rods and said: “By Pharaoh’s dignity we shall certainly be triumphant\nفَاَ لْقٰى مُوْسٰى عَصَاهُ فَاِذَا هِىَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَاْفِكُوْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(45)\nFA-ALQEEHE LQAA MOOSAA A’ASAAHU FA-EZAA HEYA TALQAFU MAA YAAFEKOONA.\nThen cast down Moses his staff, and lo! it swallowed that which they falsely displayed.\nفَاُلْقِىَ السَّحَرَةُ سٰجِدِيْنَۙ‏(46)\nFA ULQEYA AS-SAHARATU SAAJEDEENA.\nThen flung themselves the sorcerers prostrating.\nقَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(47)\nQAALOO AAMANNAA BE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSaid (the sorcerers): “Believe we in the Lord of the worlds!\nرَبِّ مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(48)\nRABBE MOOSAA WA AALO.\nThe Lord of Moses and Aaron!\nقَالَ اٰمَنْتُمْ لَهٗ قَبْلَ اَنْ اٰذَنَ لَكُمْ‌ۚ اِنَّهٗ لَكَبِيْرُكُمُ الَّذِىْ عَلَّمَكُمُ السِّحْرَ‌ۚ فَلَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ لَاُقَطِّعَنَّ اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ وَّلَاُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(49)\nQAALA AAMANTUM LAHU QABLA AN AAAZANA LAKUM INNAHU LAKABEERUKUMU LAZEE A’ALLAMAKUMU SEHR FALASAWFA TA’LAMOON LAAQATTEA’ANNA AAYDEEKUM WAARJULAKUM MIN KHELAAFIN WWALAASALLEBANNAKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nSaid (Pharaoh): “What! Believe ye unto him ere I give you leave; Verily, he is the chief of you who taught you the sorcery; so soon shall ye know; then certainly, will I cut off your hands and your feet on opposite side, and certainly will I crucify you all\nقَالُوْا لَا ضَيْرَ‌ اِنَّاۤ اِلٰى رَبِّنَا مُنْقَلِبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(50)\nQAALOO LAA ZAYRA INNAA ELAA RABBENAA MUNQALEBOONA.\nSaid they: “No harm; Verily we unto our Lord shall return.\nاِنَّا نَطْمَعُ اَنْ يَّغْفِرَ لَنَا رَبُّنَا خَطٰيٰنَاۤ اَنْ كُنَّاۤ اَوَّلَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(51)\nINNAA NATMAU’U AN YAGHFERAL LANAA RABBONAA KHATAAYAANAA AN KUNNAA AWWALA AL-MUMENEENA.\nVerily we hope that our Lord will pardon us our wrongs for we are the first of the believers.\nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اَنْ اَسْرِ بِعِبَادِىْۤ اِنَّكُمْ مُّتَّبَعُوْنَ‏(52)\nWA AWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA AN AASRE BE-E’BAADEE INNAKUM MUTTABA-O’ONA.\nAnd revealed We unto Moses (saying): “Go thou forth with My servants by night, for verily ye will be pursued.\nفَاَرْسَلَ فِرْعَوْنُ فِى الْمَدَآئِنِ حٰشِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\nFA ARSALA FIRA’WNO FIL AL-MADAAENE HAASHEREENA.\nThen sent Pharaoh in the cities, (his) heralds.\nاِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ لَشِرْذِمَةٌ قَلِيْلُوْنَۙ‏(54)\nINNAL HAAOOLAAA-E LASHERZEMATUN QALEELOONA.\n(And said he) “Verily these (Israelites) are only a small group”,\nوَاِنَّهُمْ لَنَا لَغَآئِظُوْنَۙ‏(55)\nWA INNAHUM LANAA LAGHAAEZOONA.\nVerily they unto us have enraged very much”,\nوَاِنَّا لَجَمِيْعٌ حٰذِرُوْنَؕ‏(56)\nWA INNAA LAJAMEEA’UN HAAZEROONA.\nAnd verily We are a multitude forewarned (and well Provided)\nفَاَخْرَجْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(57)\nFAAKHRAJNAAHUM MIN JANNAATIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nSo We turned them out of the gardens and the springs,\nوَّكُنُوْزٍ وَّمَقَامٍ كَرِيْمٍۙ‏(58)\nWWAKUNOOZIN WA MAQAAMIN KAREEM.\nAnd treasures and goodly dwelling,\nكَذٰلِكَؕ وَاَوْرَثْنٰهَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَؕ‏(59)\nKA-ZAALEK WA AWRASNAAHAA BANEE AESRAAEELA.\nThus (did We punish them) and We made the children of Israel the inheritors to them.\nفَاَ تْبَعُوْهُمْ مُّشْرِقِيْنَ‏(60)\nFA-ALQEEHE TBAU’OOHUM MMUSHREQEENA.\nThen they (Pharaoh with his host) pursued them at sunrise.\nفَلَمَّا تَرَآءَ الْجَمْعٰنِ قَالَ اَصْحٰبُ مُوْسٰٓى اِنَّا لَمُدْرَكُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(61)\nFALAMMAA TARAAA AL-JAMA’AANE QAALA ASHAABUN MOOSAA INNAA LAMUDRAKOONA.\nWhen the two parties saw each other, said those with Moses: “Indeed we are caught!\nقَالَ كَلَّا‌‌ ۚ اِنَّ مَعِىَ رَبِّىْ سَيَهْدِيْنِ‏(62)\nQAALA KALLAA INNAL MA-E’YA RABBEE SAYAHDEENE.\n(Moses) said: “By no means! verily my Lord is with me, soon will He guide me (to safety).\nفَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اَنِ اضْرِبْ بِّعَصَاكَ الْبَحْرَ‌ؕ فَانْفَلَقَ فَكَانَ كُلُّ فِرْقٍ كَالطَّوْدِ الْعَظِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(63)\nFAAWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA SAALEHAN AZREB BE-A’SAAKAL AL-BAHRA FAANFALAQA FA KAANA KULLO FERQIN KAALTTAWDE A’ZEEM.\nThen revealed We unto Moses saying: “Strike thou the sea with thy staff”; then it clave asunder and each part (of the water stood) like a huge mountain.\nوَاَزْلَفْنَا ثَمَّ الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(64)\nWAAZLAFNAA SUMMA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We drew near the others\nوَاَنْجَيْنَا مُوْسٰى وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(65)\nWA ANJAYNAL MOOSAA WA MAN MMAA’AH AJMA-E’ENA.\nAnd saved We Moses and those with him all of them.\nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ؕ‏(66)\nSUMMA AAGHRAQNAA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We drowned the others.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً ‌ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(67)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nVerily in this is a sure sign; but most of them believe not.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(68)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd verily thy Lord, certainly He is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful.\nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‌ۘ‏(69)\nWAATLU A’LAYHIM NABAA IBRAAHEEMA.\nAnd recite unto them the story of Abraham.\nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(70)\nIZ QAALA LEAABEEHE WA QAWMEHI MAA TA’BODOONA.\nWhen said he unto his father and his people: “What do ye worship?\nقَالُوْا نَعْبُدُ اَصْنَامًا فَنَظَلُّ لَهَا عٰكِفِيْنَ‏(71)\nQAALOO NA’BODO AASNAAMAN FANAZALLU LAHAA A’AAKEFEENA.\nSaid they: “Worship we the idols, and we shall ever be unto them the devotees.\nقَالَ هَلْ يَسْمَعُوْنَكُمْ اِذْ تَدْعُوْنَۙ‏(72)\nQAALA HAL YASMAU’OONAKUM IZ TADU’OONA.\nSaid (Abraham): “Do they hear you when ye call (them)?\nاَوْ يَنْفَعُوْنَكُمْ اَوْ يَضُرُّوْنَ‏(73)\nAW YANFAU’OONAKUM AW YAZURROONA.\nOr do they profit you (in any way) or cause you (any) harm?\nقَالُوْا بَلْ وَجَدْنَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا كَذٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(74)\nQAALOO BAL WAJADNAA AABAAA-ANAA KAZAALEKA YAF-A’LOON.\nSaid they: “Nay! found we our fathers likewise acting.\nقَالَ اَفَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّا كُنْتُمْ تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(75)\nQAALA AFA-RA-AYTUM MAA KUNTUM TA’BODOONA.\nHave ye then seen what ye have been worshipping?\nاَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمُ الْاَقْدَمُوْنَ ‌ۖ ‏(76)\nANTUM WAABAAUKUMU AL-AAQDAMOONA.\nYe and your fathers ancient?\nفَاِنَّهُمْ عَدُوٌّ لِّىْۤ اِلَّا رَبَّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(77)\nFA INNAHUM A’DUWWUM LEE ILLAA LAZEE HARRAMAHAA A’ALAMEEN.\nVerily they are enemies unto me, save the Lord of the worlds,\nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَنِىْ فَهُوَ يَهْدِيْنِۙ‏(78)\nLAZEE KHALAQANEAA FAHOWA YAHDEENE.\nWho created me, and He it is who guideth me,\nوَ الَّذِىْ هُوَ يُطْعِمُنِىْ وَيَسْقِيْنِۙ‏(79)\nWA LAZEE HOWA YUTE’EMUNEAA WAYASQEENE.\nAnd who feedeth me provideth me to drink.\nوَاِذَا مَرِضْتُ فَهُوَ يَشْفِيْنِ ۙ‏(80)\nWA EZAA MAREZTU FAHOWA YASHFEENE.\nAnd when I get ill then He healeth me,\nوَالَّذِىْ يُمِيْتُنِىْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيْنِۙ‏(81)\nWAL LAZEE YUMEETUNEAA SUMMA YUHYEENE.\nAnd who causeth me to die and then giveth me life (again),\nوَالَّذِىْۤ اَطْمَعُ اَنْ يَّغْفِرَ لِىْ خَطِٓیْئَتِىْ يَوْمَ الدِّيْنِ ؕ‏(82)\nWAL LAZEE AATMAU’U AN YAGHFERAL LEE KHATEAAATEAA YAWMA DEENE.\nAnd Who, hope I, will forgive me my faults on the Day of Judgment.\nرَبِّ هَبْ لِىْ حُكْمًا وَّاَلْحِقْنِىْ بِالصّٰلِحِيْنَۙ‏(83)\nRABBE HAB LEE HUKMAWN WWAALHEQNEAA BE-SAALEHEEN.\nO’ My Lord! Grant thou unto me authority and unite me with the righteous!\nوَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(84)\nWA A’L LEE LESAANA SEDQIN FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd cause for me a Truthful tongue (goodly mention) among the posterity.\nوَاجْعَلْنِىْ مِنْ وَّرَثَةِ جَنَّةِ النَّعِيْمِۙ‏(85)\nWAAJA’ALNEAA MIN WWARASATE JANNATE NA-E’EM.\nAnd make me of the heirs of the garden of Bliss,\nوَاغْفِرْ لِاَبِىْۤ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الضَّآلِّيْنَۙ‏(86)\nFIRLANAA LE-ABEE INNAHU KAANA MENAL ZAAL-LEEN.\nAnd forgive my father, verily, he was of those who have gone astray,\nوَلَا تُخْزِنِىْ يَوْمَ يُبْعَثُوْنَۙ‏(87)\nWA LAA TUKHZENEAA YAWMA YUB-A’SOON.\nAnd disgrace me not on the day when they are raised (again),\nيَوْمَ لَا يَنْفَعُ مَالٌ وَّلَا بَنُوْنَۙ‏(88)\nYAWMA LAA YANFAU’N MAALUN WA LAA BANOONA.\nThe day when will avail not wealth or sons,\nاِلَّا مَنْ اَتَى اللّٰهَ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيْمٍؕ‏(89)\nILLAA MAN AATAA LAAHA BEQALBIN SALEEMIN.\nSave him who cometh unto God with a heart submissive.\nوَاُزْلِفَتِ الْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(90)\nWAAZLEFATE JANNATO LILMUTTAQEEN.\nAnd shall be brought near, the garden for the pious ones.\nوَبُرِّزَتِ الْجَحِيْمُ لِلْغٰوِيْنَۙ‏(91)\nWABURREZATE EZAL JAHEEMO LIL-GHAAWEENA.\nAnd the Hell shall lay open for those who go astray,\nوَقِيْلَ لَهُمْ اَيْنَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(92)\nWA QEELAD LAHUM AYNAMAA KUNTUM TA’BODOONA.\nAnd it shall be said unto them: “Where are those whom ye used to worship,\nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِؕ هَلْ يَنْصُرُوْنَكُمْ اَوْ يَنْتَصِرُوْنَؕ‏(93)\nMIN DOONIL LAAH HAL YANSUROONAKUM AW YANTASEROONA.\nBesides God; can they help you or help themselves?\nفَكُبْكِبُوْا فِيْهَا هُمْ وَالْغَاوٗنَۙ‏(94)\nFAKUBKEBOOA FEEHAA HUM WAL GHAAWNA.\nSo they shall be thrown down into it, they and those gone astray,\nوَجُنُوْدُ اِبْلِيْسَ اَجْمَعُوْنَؕ‏(95)\nWA JONOODUS AEBLEESA AAJMAU’OONA.\nAnd the hosts of the Iblis (Satan), all together.\nقَالُوْا وَهُمْ فِيْهَا يَخْتَصِمُوْنَۙ‏(96)\nQAALOO WA HUM FEEHAA YAKHTASEMOON.\nThey shall say, while they wrangle therein among them selves,\nتَاللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنَّا لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(97)\nTAALLLAAHE IN KUNNAA LAFEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nBy God! we were in plain error,\nاِذْ نُسَوِّيْكُمْ بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(98)\nIZ NUSAWYKUM BE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhen we equalled you with the Lord of the worlds,\nوَمَاۤ اَضَلَّنَاۤ اِلَّا الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(99)\nWA MAA AAZALLANAA ILLAA MUJREMOON.\nAnd none beguiled us but the guilty ones,\nفَمَا لَنَا مِنْ شٰفِعِيْنَۙ‏(100)\nFAMAA LANAA MIN SHAAFEE’EENA.\nNow we have no intercessors,\nوَلَا صَدِيْقٍ حَمِيْمٍ‏(101)\nWA LAA SADEEQIN HAMEEMIN.\nNor any loving friend,\nفَلَوْ اَنَّ لَنَا كَرَّةً فَنَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(102)\nFA LAW ANNAL LANAA KARRATAN FANAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd if there be for us a return, we would be of the believers.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(103)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nVerily in this is a sign; And most of them believe not.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(104)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd verily thy Lord, He is certainly the All-Mighty, All- Merciful.\nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ نُوْحِۨالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(105)\nKAZZABAT QAWMO NOOHEALMURSALEENA.\nThe people of Noah belied the apostles (of God),\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ نُوْحٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(106)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AAKHOOHUM NOOHUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen said unto them their brother Noah: “Will ye not guard (yourselves) against evil?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(107)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nVerily I am unto you a trusted apostle,\nفَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَ اَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(108)\nFAT-TAQUN LAAHA WA AATEEU’OONE.\nGuard ye therefore against (the wrath of) God, and obey me;\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(109)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd I ask not from you any recompense for it, for my recompense is only with the Lord of the worlds.\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ ؕ‏(110)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nSo guard ye (yourselves) against (the wrath of) God, and obey me\nقَالُوْۤا اَنُؤْمِنُ لَكَ وَاتَّبَعَكَ الْاَرْذَلُوْنَؕ‏(111)\nQAALOO A-NOAMENO LAKA WAATTABAA’AKA AL-AARZALOONA.\nSaid they: “What! Shall we believe in thee, while follow thee the meanest (ones)?\nقَالَ وَمَا عِلْمِىْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(112)\nQAALA WA MAA E’ELMEAA BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nSaid (Noah); “No knowledge have I of what they were doing;\nاِنْ حِسَابُهُمْ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّىْ‌ لَوْ تَشْعُرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(113)\nIN HESAABUHUM ILLAA A’LAA RABBEE LAW TASH-O’ROON.\nTheir reckoning is only on my Lord, if ye only knew\nوَمَاۤ اَنَا بِطَارِدِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(114)\nWA MAA ANAA BETAAREDE MOAMENEEN.\nI am not here to drive away the believers.\nاِنْ اَنَا اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌؕ‏(115)\nIN ANAA ILLAA NAZEERUM MMUBEENUN.\nI am not but an open warner\nقَالُوْا لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ يٰنُوْحُ لَتَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمَرْجُوْمِيْنَؕ‏(116)\nQAALOO LAIL LAM TANTAHE YAANOOHU LATAKOONANNA MENAL AL-MARJOOMEENA.\nSaid (they): “Now, if thou desist not, O’ Noah! thou shalt surely be one of those stoned to death.\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنَّ قَوْمِىْ كَذَّبُوْنِ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(117)\nQAALA RABBE INNAL QAWMEE KAZZABOONE.\nSaid (Noah): “My Lord! verily my people have belied me\nفَافْتَحْ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ فَتْحًا وَّنَجِّنِىْ وَمَنْ مَّعِىَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(118)\nFAAFTAH BAYNEE WA BAYNAHUM FATHAN WWANAJJENEAA WA MAN MA-E’YA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nTherefore decide thou a decision between me and them, and deliver me and those of the believers with me,\nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗ فِى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(119)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO WA MAN MMAA’AH FIL FULKE MASH-HOON.\nSo We delivered him and those with him in the laden Ark\nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا بَعْدُ الْبٰقِيْنَؕ‏(120)\nSUMMA AAGHRAQNAA BA’DO AL-BAAQEENA.\nThen drowned We the rest afterwards.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(121)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nVerily in this is a sign; but most of them believe not.\nوَ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(122)\nWA INNAL RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nVerily thy Lord, certainly He is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful.\nكَذَّبَتْ عَادُ اۨلْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ‌ۖ ‌ۚ‏(123)\nKAZZABAT A’AADU MURSALEEN.\nThe (people) ’Ad belied the apostles (of God),\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ هُوْدٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(124)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AAKHOOHUM HOODUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen said unto them their brother Hud: “Will ye not guard (yourselves) against evil?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌ‌ۙ‏(125)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nVerily I, unto you, am a trusted apostle,\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(126)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore guard ye (yourselves) against (the wrath of) God, and obey me\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(127)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nI seek not from you any recompense for it, for my recompense is only with the Lord of the worlds\nاَتَبْنُوْنَ بِكُلِّ رِيْعٍ اٰيَةً تَعْبَثُوْنَۙ‏(128)\nAATABNOONA BEKULLE REEA’IN AAYATAL TAA’BASOONA.\nBuild ye on every height a monument? (but) vain it is,\nوَ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(129)\nWA TATTAKHEZOONA MASAANEA’A LA-A’LLAKUM TAKHLUDOONA.\nAnd raise ye strong mansions as if ye will abide (therein) for ever.\nوَاِذَا بَطَشْتُمْ بَطَشْتُمْ جَبَّارِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(130)\nWA EZAA BATASHTUM BATASHTUM JABBAAREENA.\nAnd when ye seize (any one) by force, ye seize as tyrants\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(131)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nSo guard ye (yourselves) against (the wrath of) God, and obey me,\nوَاتَّقُوْا الَّذِىْۤ اَمَدَّكُمْ بِمَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(132)\nWAT TAQOO LAZEE AAMADDAKUM BEMAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd fear ye Him who hath bestowed plenty on you, what ye know\nاَمَدَّكُمْ بِاَنْعَامٍ وَّبَنِيْنَ ‌ۚۙ‏(133)\nAAMADDAKUM BEAANA’AAMIN WWABANEENA.\nHe hath provided you with plenty of cattle and children,\nوَجَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍ‌ۚ‏(134)\nWA JANNAATIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nAnd gardens and springs,\nاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍؕ‏(135)\nINNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’AZEEMIN.\nVerily I fear for you against the chastisement of a grievous day.\nقَالُوْا سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْنَاۤ اَوَعَظْتَ اَمْ لَمْ تَكُنْ مِّنَ الْوٰعِظِيْنَۙ‏(136)\nQAALOO SAWAAA-UN A’LAYNAA AAWAA’AZTA AM LAM TAKUN MENAL AL-WAAE’EZEENA.\nSaid (they): “It is same to us if thou admonish us, or be not of the admonishers (unto us),\nاِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا خُلُقُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(137)\nIN HAAZAA ILLAA KHULUQU AWWALEEN.\nThis (threatening) is naught but the custom of the ancients,\nوَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(138)\nWA MAA NAHNO BEMUA’AZZABEENA.\nAnd We are not those who would be punished\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاَيَةً‌ ؕ وَ مَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(139)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FAAHLAKNAAHUM INNAL FEE ZAALEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nSo they belied him, then We destroyed them; Verily in this is a sign; but most of them believe not.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(140)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd verily thy Lord, certainly He is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful.\nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(141)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO MURSALEEN.\nBelied (the tribe of) Thamud, the apostles (of God),\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ صٰلِحٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(142)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AAKHOOHUM SAALEHUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen said unto them their brother Salih: “Will ye not guard (yourselves) against evil?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(143)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nVerily I, unto you, am a trusted apostle,\nفَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(144)\nFAT-TAQUN LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nFear ye (the wrath of) God, and obey me,\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(145)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd I seek not of you any recompense for it, for my recompense is only with the Lord of the worlds;\nاَتُتْرَكُوْنَ فِىْ مَا هٰهُنَاۤ اٰمِنِيْنَۙ‏(146)\nAATUTRAKOONA FEE MAA HAAHUNAA AAMENEENA.\nWhat! Will ye be left in what is here, secure (for ever)?\nفِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(147)\nFEE JANNAATIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nIn the gardens and springs,\nوَّزُرُوْعٍ وَّنَخْلٍ طَلْعُهَا هَضِيْمٌ‌ۚ‏(148)\nWA ZOROO-I’NW WWANAKHLIN TALU’UHAA HAZEEMUN.\nAnd cornfields and palm-trees with fine species!\nوَتَنْحِتُوْنَ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوْتًا فٰرِهِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(149)\nWATANHETOONA MENAL JEBAALE BUYOOTAN FAAREHEENA.\nAnd ye hew out of the mountains for dwellings (for you), exaltingly\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(150)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore, fear ye (the wrath of) God, and obey me,\nوَلَا تُطِيْعُوْۤا اَمْرَ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَۙ‏(151)\nWA LAA TO-TEE-O’O AAMRA MUSREFEEN.\nAnd obey not the bidding of the extravagants,\nالَّذِيْنَ يُفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَ لَا يُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(152)\nLAZEENA YUFSEDOONA FIL ARZE WA LAA LAA YUSLEHOON.\nThose who make mischief in the earth, and amend not.\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مِنَ الْمُسَحَّرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(153)\nQAALOO INNAMAA ANTA MENAL AL-MUSAHHAREENA.\nSaid they: “verily thou art only of the bewitched ones,\nمَاۤ اَنْتَ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا ‌ ۖۚ فَاْتِ بِاٰيَةٍ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(154)\nMAA ANTA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLONAA FAATE BE-AAYATIL IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nThou art naught but a man like unto us, so bring thou a sign if thou art one of the truthful (ones)\nقَالَ هٰذِهٖ نَاقَةٌ لَّهَا شِرْبٌ وَّلَكُمْ شِرْبُ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍ‌ۚ‏(155)\nQAALA HAAZEHI NAAQATUN LLAHAA SHERBUN WWALAKUM SHERBU YAWMIN MA’LOOM.\nSaid (Salih) “Behold ye! This is a She-Camel for it shall be its drink and for you shall be your drink, (each) on an appointed day.\nوَلَا تَمَسُّوْهَا بِسُوْٓءٍ فَيَاْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(156)\nWA LAA TAMASSOOHAA BE-SOOO-IN FAYAAKHUZAKUM A’ZAABO YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nTouch her not with evil, lest will seize you the torment of the grievous day.\nفَعَقَرُوْهَا فَاَصْبَحُوْا نٰدِمِيْنَۙ‏(157)\nFA-A’QAROOHAA FA-ASBAHOO NAADEMEENA.\nThen they hamstrung her, and turned (themselves) regretful,\nفَاَخَذَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(158)\nTOOFAANO A’ZAAB INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nSo seized them the chastisement; verily in this there is a sign; but most of them believe not.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(159)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd verily thy Lord, He is certainly the All-Mighty, The All-Merciful.\nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ اۨلْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(160)\nKAZZABAT QAWMO LOOTIM MURSALEEN.\nBelied the people of Lut, the apostles (of God)\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ لُوْطٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(161)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AAKHOOHUM LOOT ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen said unto them their brother Lut: “Will ye not guard {yourselves) against evil?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(162)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nVerily I, unto you, am a trusted apostle,\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(163)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore fear ye (the wrath of) God, and obey me,\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(164)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nI seek not from you for it any recompense, for my recompense is only on the Lord of the worlds.\nاَتَاْتُوْنَ الذُّكْرَانَ مِنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(165)\nATAATOONAL AZ-ZUKRAANA MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhat! come ye (only) to males, of all the creatures!\nوَ تَذَرُوْنَ مَا خَلَقَ لَكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ مِّنْ اَزْوَاجِكُمْ‌ؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ عٰدُوْنَ‏(166)\nWA TAZAROONA MAA KHALAQAL LAKUM RABBOKUM MIN AAZWAAJEKUM BAL ANTUM QAWMUN A’AADOONA.\nAnd leave ye what hath created for you your Lord, of your wives? Nay! ye are people transgressing (the limits)\nقَالُوْا لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ يٰلُوْطُ لَتَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُخْرَجِيْنَ‏(167)\nQAALOO LAIL LAM TANTAHE YAALOOTU LATAKOONANNA MENAL AL-MUKHRAJEENA.\nSaid they: “If thou desist not O’ Lut! thou shalt surely be of those who are expelled.\nقَالَ اِنِّىْ لِعَمَلِكُمْ مِّنَ الْقَالِيْنَؕ‏(168)\nQAALA INNEE LEA’AMALEKUM MENAL AL-QAALEENA.\nSaid (Lut): “Verily, I am of those who abhor your doings\nرَبِّ نَجِّنِىْ وَاَهْلِىْ مِمَّا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(169)\nRABBE NAJJENEE WAAHLEAA MIMMAA YA’MALOON.\nMy Lord! “deliver me and my family from what they do!\nفَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَ اَهْلَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(170)\nFANAJJAYNAAHU WA AHLAHU AJMA-E’ENA.\nSo, We did deliver him and his people, all,\nاِلَّا عَجُوْزًا فِى الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(171)\nILLAA A’AJOOZAN FIL GHAABEREEN.\nSave an old woman among those who tarried behind.\nثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(172)\nSUMMA DAMMARNAA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We destroyed the others.\nوَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّطَرًا‌ۚ فَسَآءَ مَطَرُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(173)\n58 WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHIM MATARAA FA-SAAA-A MATARUL MUNZEREEN.\nAnd we showered down, upon them, and evil was the rain on those (who were) warned (but heeded not).\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً‌  ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(174)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nVerily in this is a sign, but most of them believe not.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(175)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd verily thy Lord, certainly He is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful.\nكَذَّبَ اَصْحٰبُ لْئَيْكَةِ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ‌ۖ‌ۚ‏(176)\nKAZZABA ASHAABUN LAYKATE MURSALEEN.\nBelied the dwellers of the forest, the apostles (of God)\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ شُعَيْبٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(177)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM SHUA’AYBUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen said unto them Shu’ayb: Not to cheat people of their things “Will ye not guard (yourselves) against evil.\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(178)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nVerily I unto you am a trusted apostle,\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(179)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nSo fear ye (the wrath of) God and obey me\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(180)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nI seek not from you, for it any compensation, for my compensation is only on the Lord of the worlds.\nاَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا مِنَ الْمُخْسِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(181)\nAAWFOOA AL-KAYLA WA LAA TAKOONOO MENAL AL-MUKHSEREENA.\nGive ye just measure and be not of those who lessen (to deceive)\nوَزِنُوْا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(182)\nWAZENOOA BIL-QESTAASE AL-MUSTAQEEME.\nAnd weigh with balances correct, upright\nوَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ اَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(183)\nWA LAA TABKHASOOA NAASA AASHYAAAHUM WA LAA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\nDefraud not people in their (due) goods, and work not evil in the earth making mischief\nوَاتَّقُوا الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ وَالْجِبِلَّةَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَؕ‏(184)\nWAT TAQUL LAZEE KHALAQAKUM WAL JEBELLATA AWWALEEN.\nFear Him who created you and the races of old\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مِنَ الْمُسَحَّرِيْنَۙ‏(185)\nQAALOO INNAMAA ANTA MENAL AL-MUSAHHAREENA.\nSaid they: “Verily thou art only of those bewitched,\nوَمَاۤ اَنْتَ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا وَ اِنْ نَّظُنُّكَ لَمِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(186)\nWA MAA ANTA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLONAA WA IN NNAZUNNUKA LAMENAS KAAZEBEEN.\nThou art but a man like us, and we deem thee certainly of the liars;\nفَاَسْقِطْ عَلَيْنَا كِسَفًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَؕ‏(187)\nFAASQET A’LAYNAA KESAFAN MENAL SAMAAA-E IN KUNTA MENAL AS-SAADEQEENA.\nCause (thou) then a part of the heaven to fall down upon us, if thou art one of the truthful (ones)\nقَالَ رَبِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(188)\nQAALA RABBEE A-A’LAMO BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nSaid (Shu’ayb): “My Lord knoweth best what (all) ye do\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَخَذَهُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمِ الظُّلَّةِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(189)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FAAKHAZAHUM A’ZAABO YAWMIL AZ-ZULLATE INNAHU KAANA A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nBut they belied him, so seized them the chastisement of the day of cloud; Verily it was a chastisement of a Mighty day.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً ‌ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(190)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nVerily in this is a sign, but most of them believe not,\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(191)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd verily thy Lord, certainly He is the All-Mighty, All-Merciful.\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَتَنْزِيْلُ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(192)\nWA INNAHU LATANZEELU RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd verily it hath come down from the Lord of the worlds.\nنَزَلَ بِهِ الرُّوْحُ الْاَمِيْنُۙ‏(193)\nNAZALA BEHIL ROOHO AMEEN.\nCame down with it the Spirit trusted,\nعَلٰى قَلْبِكَ لِتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُنْذِرِيْنَۙ‏(194)\nA’LAA QALBEKA LETAKOONA MENAL MUNZEREEN.\nUpon thy heart (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) that thou mayest be the Warner,\nبِلِسَانٍ عَرَبِىٍّ مُّبِيْنٍؕ‏(195)\nBELESAANIN A’ARABEAAAIN MMUBEENIN.\nIn the language, plain Arabic.\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَفِىْ زُبُرِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(196)\nWA INNAHU LAFEE ZUBURE AWWALEEN.\nAnd verily it is foretold in the scriptures of yore,\nاَوَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهُمْ اٰيَةً اَنْ يَّعْلَمَهٗ عُلَمٰٓؤُا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَؕ‏(197)\nAWALAM YAKUL LAHUM AAYATAL AN YYAA’LAMAH U’ULAMAAAUA BANEE AESRAAEELA.\nIs it not a sign unto them that recognize it the learned ones of the children of Israel?\nوَلَوْ نَزَّلْنٰهُ عَلٰى بَعْضِ الْاَعْجَمِيْنَۙ‏(198)\nWA LAW NAZZALNAAHU A’LAA BAA’ZE AL-AAA’JAMEENA.\nAnd if We had sent it down unto any of the outlanders,\nفَقَرَاَهٗ عَلَيْهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ مُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(199)\nFAQARAAH A’LAYHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI MUMENEENA.\n(And) then had he recited it unto them, they would have believed not in it.\nكَذٰلِكَ سَلَكْنٰهُ فِىْ قُلُوْبِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَؕ‏(200)\nKAZAALEKA SALAKNAAHU FEE QOLOOBIL AL-MUJREMEENA.\nThus We caused it passing into the hearts of the guilty (ones)\nلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ حَتّٰى يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَۙ‏(201)\nLAA YOAMENOONA BEHI HATTAA YARAWUA A’ZAABA AL-AALEEMA.\nThey will believe not in it till they see the grievous chastisement,\nفَيَاْتِيَهُمْ بَغْتَةً وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(202)\nFAYAATEEHUM BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nAnd it shall come upon them of a sudden, while they perceive not,\nفَيَقُوْلُوْا هَلْ نَحْنُ مُنْظَرُوْنَؕ‏(203)\nFAYAQOOLOO HAL NAHNO MUNZAROONA.\nThen will they say: “Shall we be respited?\nاَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(204)\nAAFABEA’AZAABENAA YASTAA’JELOONA.\nWhat! Seek they to hasten Our chastisement?\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ مَّتَّعْنٰهُمْ سِنِيْنَۙ‏(205)\nAAFARAAYTA IN MMATTAA’NAAHUM SENEEN.\nHast thou then seen that We provided them to enjoy themselves for years,\nثُمَّ جَآءَهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(206)\nSUMMA JAAA-AHUM MAA KAANOO YOOA’ADOONA.\nThen came unto them that which they were promised,\nمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يُمَتَّعُوْنَؕ‏(207)\nMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YUMATTAU’OONA.\nAvailed them not that which they were provided to enjoy.\nوَمَاۤ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍ اِلَّا لَهَا مُنْذِرُوْنَ‌‌‌‌‌ ۛ ‌ۖ ‏(208)\nWA MAA AHLAKNAL MIN QARYATINW ILLAA LAHAA MUNZEROONA.\nWe destroyed not any town but it had its warners,\nذِكْرٰى‌ۛ وَمَا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(209)\nZEKRAA WA MAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nTo Remind (them); and never are We unjust.\nوَمَا تَنَزَّلَتْ بِهِ الشَّيٰطِيْنُ‏(210)\nWA MAA TANAZZALAT BEHIL SHAYAATEENO.\nAnd came not with it, the devils.\nوَمَا يَنْۢبَغِىْ لَهُمْ وَمَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَؕ‏(211)\nWA MAA LAHAA LAHUM WA MAA YASTATEEU’OONA.\nIt behoveth them not, they can do it.\nاِنَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّمْعِ لَمَعْزُوْلُوْنَؕ‏(212)\nINNAHUM A’NIL AS-SAME’E LAMAA’ZOOLOONA.\nVerily they, (even) from hearing it, are far removed.\nفَلَا تَدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(213)\nFALAA TAD-O’ LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FA TAKOONA MENAL AL-MUA’AZZABEENA.\nSo call thou not with God another god, lest thou be of the chastised ones.\nوَاَنْذِرْ عَشِيْرَتَكَ الْاَقْرَبِيْنَۙ‏(214)\nWAANZER A’ASHEERATAKA AL-AAQRABEENA.\nAnd warn thou thy relatives of nearest kin.\nوَاخْفِضْ جَنَاحَكَ لِمَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(215)\nWAAKHFEZ JANAAHAKA LEMANIT ATTABAA’AKA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd be kind unto him who followeth thee, of the believers.\nفَاِنْ عَصَوْكَ فَقُلْ اِنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(216)\nFA-IN A’ASAWKA FAQUL INNEE BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TA’MALOON.\nBut if they disobey thee, then say: “verily I disassociate (myself) of what ye do!\nوَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْعَزِيْزِ الرَّحِيْمِۙ‏(217)\nWA TAWAKKAL A’LAL A’ZEEZIL RAHEEM.\nAnd rely thou on Mighty, All-Merciful,\nالَّذِىْ يَرٰٮكَ حِيْنَ تَقُوْمُۙ‏(218)\nLAZEE YARAAKA HEENA YAQOOMUS.\nHe who seeth thee when thou dost stand up,\nوَتَقَلُّبَكَ فِى السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(219)\nWATAQALLUBAKA FIL AS-SAAJEDEENA.\nAnd thy movements among those who prostrate themselves (in obeisance unto God)\nاِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(220)\nINNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nVerily He is the All-Hearing, The All-Knowing,\nهَلْ اُنَبِّئُكُمْ عَلٰى مَنْ تَنَزَّلُ الشَّيٰطِيْنُؕ‏(221)\nHAL AUNABBEUKUM A’LAA MAN TANAZZALUL ASH-SHAYTEENU.\nShall I inform you (of him) upon whom descend the satans?\nتَنَزَّلُ عَلٰى كُلِّ اَفَّاكٍ اَثِيْمٍۙ‏(222)\nTANAZZALUL A’LAA KULLE AAFFAAKIN ASEEM.\nDescend they on every lying sinful one,\nيُّلْقُوْنَ السَّمْعَ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ كٰذِبُوْنَؕ‏(223)\nYYULQOONA JA-A’LA WA AKSAROHUM KAAZEBOONA.\nLend they their ears (eagerly), and most of them are liars.\nوَالشُّعَرَآءُ يَتَّبِعُهُمُ الْغَاوٗنَؕ‏(224)\nWAALSSHUA’ARAAU YATTABEU’UHUMU AL-GHAAWNA.\nAnd the poets, follow them the erring ones,\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّهُمْ فِىْ كُلِّ وَادٍ يَّهِيْمُوْنَۙ‏(225)\nALAM TARA ANNAHUM FEE KULLE WAADIN YYAHEEMOONA.\nSee thou not that they, in every valley they wander bewildered?\nوَاَنَّهُمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ مَا لَا يَفْعَلُوْنَۙ‏(226)\nWA ANNAHUM YAQOOLOONA MAA LAA YAF-A’LOON.\nAnd that they say what they (themselves) do not do.\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَذَكَرُوا اللّٰهَ كَثِيْرًا وَّانْتَصَرُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا ظُلِمُوْا‌ ؕ وَسَيَعْلَمُ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَىَّ مُنْقَلَبٍ يَّنْقَلِبُوْنَ‏(227)\nILLAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WAZAKAROOA LAAHA KASEERAA WWAANTASAROOA MIN BA’DE MAA ZULEMOOA WASAYAA’LAMU LAZEENA ZALAMOO AAA MUNQALABIN YYANQALEBOONA.\nSave those who believe and do good, and remember God much, and defend themselves after they are oppressed; And soon shall know those who deal unjustly, what an (evil) turning they shall be turned unto!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Shoaraa (The Poets)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has a total of 227 verses. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites the three Tawaseen (i.e. the three Surahs beginning with Taa-Seen) on every Thursday night, will be counted from the friends of Allah and will be under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.). The reward for reciting this Surah is so great that when the person sees the reward he has gotten from it (on the Day of Judgement) he will be pleased.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will come out of his grave reciting the Shahadah or Kalimah, bearing witness in the Oneness of Allah (s.w.t.). Reciting Surah al-Shoaraa at dawn is compared to the recitation of all the heavenly books that have been revealed. Frequent recitation of this Surah ensures protection from thieves and from death by drowning or being burnt. Drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved protects one from all types of ailments."
